SlicerX is its own slicer. Its slicing engine and user interface are written
for SlicerX and contain no code or help text from OrcaSlicer, Bambu Studio,
PrusaSlicer or Slic3r. Setting key names follow the ones those slicers use so
that profiles and project files interchange, and SlicerX reads a user's own
OrcaSlicer, Bambu Studio and PrusaSlicer profile and 3MF files.

Third-party code, data and fonts keep their own licenses. THIRD-PARTY.md lists
what ships and under which terms, including the three libraries vendored in
packages/vendor with our changes (i_overlay, boostvoronoi, cpp_map), the STEP
reader built from occt-import-js and Open CASCADE Technology (LGPL-2.1; SlicerX
makes use of facilities provided by the Open CASCADE Technology software; the
source offer is in packages/vendor/occt-import-js/SOURCE.md), Cisco's OpenH264
binary, which is downloaded on Linux and never bundled, and the SigLIP2 model
weights used by the print watch. The full per-version list is generated at
release time into THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES and shipped with every build.

The aegis wall generator follows the method of preFlight's Athena walls, with
thanks to the preFlight authors. SlicerX contains none of their code.

